# Coderrr — supported environment variables
#
# IMPORTANT: Coderrr does not read .env files. It reads these from the process
# environment. This file documents the contract and gives you something to
# source; it is not loaded automatically.
#
#     cp .env.example .env       # then edit
#     set -a && . ./.env && set +a && coderrr run "..."
#
# Reading .env from a project directory was avoided deliberately: that is the
# directory the agent edits, and a plaintext key there is one `git add .` away
# from being published. Prefer either of these instead:
#
#     coderrr config                        # OS keyring, or config.toml at 0600
#     export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...          # transient, nothing on disk
#
# Precedence when Coderrr resolves a key:
#     environment variable  ->  OS keyring  ->  ~/.coderrr/config.toml


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider credentials — set only the one you use
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Anthropic (Claude)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI (GPT)
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Google (Gemini)
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — many models behind one key
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Ollama — only needed for Ollama-hosted (cloud) models. Local models need no key.
OLLAMA_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything else lives in ~/.coderrr/config.toml, not here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Provider, model, endpoint, retry limits, verification mode and sandbox tier
# are all configured in that file. Run `coderrr config` to set it up, or see the
# Configuration section of README.md for the full schema.
#
# There is no CODERRR_BACKEND variable in v2. The CLI calls providers directly;
# the hosted backend that v1 used no longer exists.
